    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 0. What this is, and what it supersedes",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZG002",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "text": "`Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` conflated two different traversal shapes under one\nwrong name — a depth-bounded recursive walk it called \"BFS Traversal\" is actually depth-first\n(IDDFS-shaped, once bounded), not breadth-first. This doc replaces it: three distinct tools,\ncorrectly named, plus a third capability (keyword/regex search) every earlier revision flagged\nas missing but never built. Together they answer \"what does an agent or human have to find a\nnode or explore the graph,\" per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A's Agentic Interface\nconcept and the gap first identified in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 1. Three distinct tools, not one",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZG003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZG004",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZG004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR000",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR001",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR002"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG003",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004/props/StringProp/otc55V8C2Ldgwyy2",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004/props/StringProp/vNOSjlbdUEAVeYFg",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "- **`kg:tree`** — a deep structural map: recursively lists nodes across many levels, optionally\n  depth-bounded. Algorithmically a depth-first walk with an optional depth cutoff —\n  IDDFS-shaped, not BFS. Good for getting oriented across a large chunk of the KG at a glance.\n- **`kg:unfold`** (and its inverse, `kg:fold`) — true breadth-first: given one node, show its\n  own `title` plus the full `text` of each of its immediate children (first level only) — no\n  recursion, no depth param, since \"first level\" is the whole point. Named `fold`/`unfold` (not\n  `collapse`/`expand`) to match the ontology's own existing vocabulary — see §3, this is also\n  the first thing to ever give the long-inert `unfolded` schema field (§4: promoted from\n  `BlockNode` to `BaseNode`) a real effect.\n  This is the real analog of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 3's \"BFS tool calls to\n  expand subtrees\": a single frontier-expansion step an agent calls repeatedly, choosing which\n  child to unfold next based on what it just read.\n- **`kg:search`** — keyword/regex content search, matched server-side via WOQL. Not structural\n  at all — finds nodes by matching a pattern against content, regardless of position in the\n  tree. Closes the gap every earlier revision of this design named and left open.",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR000",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR000",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004",
    "text": "**`kg:tree`** — a deep structural map: recursively lists nodes across many levels, optionally\n  depth-bounded. Algorithmically a depth-first walk with an optional depth cutoff —\n  IDDFS-shaped, not BFS. Good for getting oriented across a large chunk of the KG at a glance.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR001",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR001",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004",
    "text": "**`kg:unfold`** (and its inverse, `kg:fold`) — true breadth-first: given one node, show its\n  own `title` plus the full `text` of each of its immediate children (first level only) — no\n  recursion, no depth param, since \"first level\" is the whole point. Named `fold`/`unfold` (not\n  `collapse`/`expand`) to match the ontology's own existing vocabulary — see §3, this is also\n  the first thing to ever give the long-inert `unfolded` schema field (§4: promoted from\n  `BlockNode` to `BaseNode`) a real effect.\n  This is the real analog of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 3's \"BFS tool calls to\n  expand subtrees\": a single frontier-expansion step an agent calls repeatedly, choosing which\n  child to unfold next based on what it just read.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR002",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR002",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG004",
    "text": "**`kg:search`** — keyword/regex content search, matched server-side via WOQL. Not structural\n  at all — finds nodes by matching a pattern against content, regardless of position in the\n  tree. Closes the gap every earlier revision of this design named and left open.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 2. A real implementation gap this surfaced, fixed directly in `astParser.ts`",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR004",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR005",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR006",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR007",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR008",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR009"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003/props/StringProp/VGwC18BFUS-6qGUI",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003/props/StringProp/t4571Zo07EeN3uDh",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Designing `kg:unfold` (§3) exposed a missed gap in already-shipped ingestion behavior, not just\na display-layer choice: `heading` and `blockquote`/`listItem` were all being treated as\nequally content-less containers (`text = \"\"`), but they aren't equally opaque —",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR004",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR004",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "A `heading`'s real content lives in its children, but per the folding philosophy (\"a block's\n  children fold into its text (abstract)\"), it should still carry an abstract of its own, the\n  same way `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` already do via `extractAbstract`. It didn't — it was\n  hardcoded to `\"\"` regardless.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR005",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR005",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "A `listItem` is a real semantic unit (like a heading's section, just one level down), so it\n  deserves the same treatment — also missing.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR006",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR006",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "A `list` genuinely has no content of its own — its children (`listItem`s) are the actual\n  content units. It's the *only* true content-less container.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR007",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR007",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "A `blockquote` is a quote, not a summary — its full content should be projected as-is, not\n  reduced to an abstract or emptied out.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR008",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR008",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "Fixed in `astParser.ts`'s `convertAstNode`: `heading`/`listItem` now compute `text` via\n`extractAbstract` once their `children` exist (the first paragraph found among descendants,\ncascading correctly through nesting — confirmed live: a `Sub` heading two levels down correctly\npicked up its own nearest paragraph, not an ancestor's); `list` still empties `text`; `blockquote`\nnow falls through to the ordinary leaf default (`text = rawText`, its full raw slice, quote\nmarkers included) instead of being emptied. Verified this doesn't disturb reconciliation:\n`reconcile.ts` keeps its own independent `LEAF_TYPES`/`CONTAINER_TYPES` (type-based, not\ntext-based) for Stage A/B matching, so none of this changes which nodes match how — confirmed by\nre-running `verify:phase0 -- --db` clean, both in-memory and against the live DB.",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR009",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR009",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR003",
    "text": "**Known limitation surfaced by this fix**: `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` skip re-ingestion based on file\ncontent hash — a parser-logic change like this one doesn't change any file's bytes, so already-\ningested real artifacts keep their old (empty) heading/listItem `text` until something forces\nre-ingestion. Confirmed live: re-running `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` after this fix touched zero\nartifacts. Not fixed here — a real, pre-existing gap (parser version isn't part of the\nchange-detection key), out of scope for this design.",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 3. `kg:tree` — render rule: `title`, exclusively",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "text": "An earlier revision proposed falling back to a text excerpt when `title` isn't meaningful.\nRejected: a `BlockNode`'s `title` literally *is* its own `blockId` whenever nothing has\nsummarized it yet (`astParser.ts:76`) — and that **is** the meaningful signal, not a gap to\npaper over. Seeing a raw id as a node's title tells the reader \"this node is opaque — nothing\nhas read and summarized me\" (Fractal Ontology Enhancements' AI-summarization step, still\nunbuilt per `Aperas-dev-status.md`). Extracting a text excerpt instead would hide that signal\nbehind a false sense of readability. So: print `title` uniformly for every node kind, no\nfallback branching, no special-casing for containers either — `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`\ntitles are always meaningful (dirname/filename) anyway, so the rule is genuinely uniform.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00C",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00D",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00E",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00F",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00G"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00A",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B/props/StringProp/QazG6VaC7fefxExK",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B/props/StringProp/y7tjGT2gvkqCz5tl",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Command: `kg:tree [path] [--depth N]`",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00C",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00C",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "text": "`path` optional, defaults to `.` (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`) — the full tree from\n  folders.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00D",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00D",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "text": "Same addressing as the assertion CLI: a full node id or a bare artifact/folder path, resolved\n  via the existing `resolveNodeRef` (direct-or-query, `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §2).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00E",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00E",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "text": "No depth limit by default — genuinely the full tree. `--depth N` truncates to N levels,\n  printing a `…` marker at each truncation point rather than silently stopping, so it's visibly\n  a limit, not the actual leaf.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00F",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00F",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "text": "One recursive walk handles every level uniformly — `FolderNode` (nested `FolderNode`s,\n  `ArtifactNode` references, README-derived `BlockNode` children) and `ArtifactNode` →\n  `BlockNode` tree alike; the fractal ontology means no node kind needs special-casing.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00G",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00G",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00B",
    "text": "Output: one line per node, indented by depth: `<id>  [<kind>]  <title>` — `<kind>` is\n  `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` for those, or the `BlockNode`'s own mdast `type` for blocks.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 4. `kg:unfold` / `kg:fold` — one breadth-first step, persisted",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00J",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00K",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00M",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00N",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00P",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Q",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00R",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00S"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H/props/StringProp/_vYSUqUoBxOb4Vvi",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H/props/StringProp/mL3trsX__ZJLiI4U",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Command: `kg:unfold <path>`",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00J",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00J",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "`path`: same direct-or-query addressing as everywhere else (full id or artifact/folder path).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00K",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00K",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "No depth, no recursion by design — resolves to one node, then prints its own\n  `<id>  [<kind>]  <title>` **plus**, for each of its immediate children,\n  `<id>  [<kind>]  <full text>`. Full `text` *in addition to* title, not instead of it — an\n  earlier revision of this doc worded it as \"full text, not title,\" which wrongly implied\n  dropping the title; the point was only to emphasize that children get their full content\n  here, unlike `kg:tree`'s title-only listing.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00M",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00M",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "Now that §2's fix gives `heading`/`listItem` a real abstract, only a `list` child (the one\n  true content-less container per §2) ever has nothing to show — it prints\n  `<id>  [<kind>]  (no text of its own — see kg:unfold <id>)`. Every other child kind now has\n  something real to display.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00N",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00N",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "**Persists**, not just displays: also sets `unfolded = true` on the target node — the first\n  code path to ever write `true` to that field (it's existed since early in the schema,\n  defaulted `false` on creation, carried forward by reconciliation, but never meaningfully\n  written or read — confirmed live by grepping the codebase). Implementation note: a node's\n  `children` (or, for `ArtifactNode`, its singular `root`) is a required field, so the write has\n  to resubmit the full existing document with only `unfolded` changed (fetch-then-resubmit), the\n  same pattern `tombstoneSubtree` (`reconcile.ts`) already uses for a different field.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00P",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00P",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "**`unfolded` is a `BaseNode` field, not a `BlockNode`-only one** — corrected from an earlier\n  version of this design that scoped it to `BlockNode`. That scoping was a loophole, not a\n  deliberate choice: `unfolded` was designed back when `BlockNode` was the only concrete kind,\n  and simply never got carried onto `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` when the ontology split into\n  three. There's nothing BlockNode-specific about \"has this node's children been revealed\" — an\n  `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` target is just as real a thing to fold or unfold. So `kg:unfold`/\n  `kg:fold` now have genuine, persisted effect against every node kind, not display-only\n  no-ops for two of the three (§4.1 depends on this being uniform).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00Q",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00Q",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "`kg:fold <path>` is the exact inverse: sets `unfolded = false` on the target node, no content\n  printed beyond a confirmation — there's nothing new to show by re-collapsing.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00R",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00R",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "**Composability, corrected**: an earlier revision described `kg:tree` + `kg:unfold` as\n\"composable\" but only demonstrated a *sequence* of separate calls (`tree` → `unfold x` →\n`unfold y` → ...) whose results a reader has to mentally combine — not a single artifact. What\n\"composable\" should actually mean: the *persisted* `unfolded` state left behind by a sequence of\n`kg:fold`/`kg:unfold` calls is a standing, queryable shape — \"a selectively expanded tree\" — not\njust this session's scrollback. §4.1 settles the fork this section used to leave open (should\n`kg:tree` change its default behavior, or should this be a separate command): an opt-in flag on\n`kg:tree` itself, default behavior unchanged.",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### 4.1. `kg:tree --unfolded` — rendering the combined shape",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00S",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00T",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00H",
    "text": "Decided: an opt-in flag on `kg:tree`, not a new command or a changed default — `kg:tree` without\nthe flag stays exactly the uniform title-only walk of §3; `--unfolded` swaps in a second render\nrule that reads the very state `kg:fold`/`kg:unfold` (§4) persist, so a sequence of those calls\nbecomes visible as one tree instead of separate scrollback.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00T",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00T",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00S",
    "text": "Command: `kg:tree [path] [--depth N] [--no-holders] [--unfolded]` — `--unfolded` composes with\nboth existing flags unchanged (`--depth` still a hard ceiling, `--no-holders` still transparent\nper §7.5 of `Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md`).",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00W",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00X",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Z",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR010",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR011"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00S",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V/props/StringProp/3JmC-3C1icHCoSUN",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V/props/StringProp/CagYeHY35tW3h6ug",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "text": "**Rule** (applied per node during the same recursive walk, no second pass): a node is rendered\nwith its full `text` instead of `title` exactly when *its own parent* has `unfolded === true` —\ni.e., exactly the set of nodes a real `kg:unfold <parent>` call against that parent would have\nshown. Now that `unfolded` lives on `BaseNode` (§4), this applies uniformly to `BlockNode`,\n`ArtifactNode`, and `FolderNode` alike — no kind gets special-cased. Concretely:",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00W",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00W",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "The node `kg:tree` was pointed at (the root of this particular walk) is always rendered\n  title-only, regardless of its own `unfolded` state — same convention `kg:unfold` itself already\n  uses for its own target (§4: the target's line is title, only its children get full text). A\n  tree rooted partway into an already-unfolded chain still opens on a title line.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00X",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00X",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "A node whose own `unfolded` is `true`: its children are rendered full-text (per the rule above)\n  **and** the walk recurses beneath each of them, carrying the same rule forward — a grandchild\n  gets full text too, exactly when *its* parent (this child) is itself unfolded. This is what\n  makes multiple persisted `kg:unfold` calls compose into one shape: unfolding a great-grandchild\n  earlier makes it show up expanded here too, at whatever depth it sits, and unfolding a\n  `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` reveals the abstracts of the files/subfolders inside it exactly the\n  same way unfolding a `BlockNode` reveals its children's text.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00Y",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00Y",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "A node whose own `unfolded` is not `true` (folded, including the never-unfolded default): the\n  walk does **not** descend into its children at all — they haven't been revealed, so showing\n  them would assert something no `kg:unfold` call ever established. If it has children, one line\n  is printed in their place: `…  (folded — kg:unfold <id> to expand)` — the same affordance as\n  the existing list-type message in §4, naming the exact command that would reveal them. This is\n  the \"stops at folded ones\" half of the shape, and it now applies at a folder or artifact\n  boundary too, not just inside a block tree.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR00Z",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR00Z",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "The one content-less case from §4 (a `list`-type `BlockNode`, the only kind with genuinely\n  nothing of its own) prints the same `(no text of its own — see kg:unfold <id>)` line it does in\n  `kg:unfold`'s own output, rather than an empty string.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR010",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR010",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "`--depth N` is checked first, as an unconditional ceiling — it can still truncate inside an\n  unfolded chain (printing the existing `…` marker), independent of any node's `unfolded` state.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR011",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR011",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR00V",
    "text": "A holder (`Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md` §7.5) is rendered by the same rule as any\n  other node — its `(holder)` tag is orthogonal to whether it's shown full-text or title-only, and\n  `--no-holders` keeps hiding its own line while still descending through it exactly as before.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 5. `kg:search` — keyword/regex content search",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "text": "Command: `kg:search <pattern>` — PCRE-style regex, matching `WOQL.re`'s own semantics.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR013",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR013",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR014",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR015",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR016"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR012",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013/props/StringProp/S6DV-YOI2E6zGdtR",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013/props/StringProp/m-EEObk1nQMdODiS",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Confirmed live (not just documented): TerminusDB's WOQL builder exposes\n`WOQL.re(pattern, inputVarName, resultVarList)` (`terminusdb` npm package, `lib/woql.js:1262`)\n— genuine server-side regex matching, not a client-side scan. Tested directly against the real\nKG: `WOQL.re('Assertion', titleVar, matchVar)` combined with `WOQL.triple(doc, 'title',\ntitleVar)` correctly matched 3 real `BlockNode` titles containing \"Assertion.\" A pattern with a\nregex metacharacter (`kg:\\w+`) also matched correctly using ordinary single-level JS string\nescaping — the \"escape twice\" note in the client's own docstring turned out to be about\ninternal JSON-LD wire transport, already handled by the client library; callers don't need to\ndouble-escape anything themselves.",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR014",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR014",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013",
    "text": "Searches `title` and `text` across all three node classes (`BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`,\n  `FolderNode`) — six queries (3 classes × 2 fields), each\n  `WOQL.and(WOQL.triple(v.Doc, field, v.Value), WOQL.re(pattern, v.Value, v.Match))`. A\n  class/field a given document doesn't have (e.g. `Optional text` absent) simply produces no\n  triple to match against — no special-casing needed.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR015",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR015",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013",
    "text": "`title`/`text` are `xsd:string` literals, so bindings come back wrapped\n  (`{\"@type\", \"@value\"}`), exactly like `predicate` did in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §4 — reuses the existing `unwrapLiteral` (`woql.ts`) rather than re-solving the same problem.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJJVZR016",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR016",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR013",
    "text": "Output: `<id>  [<kind>]  <field>  <value>` per match, across all six queries, deduplicated by\n  id (a node could match on both `title` and `text`).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZR017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 6. Phase placement — decided",
    "blockId": "00C7BJJVZR017",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJJVZG001",
    "text": "Confirmed: moved into Phase 0, same reasoning as Artifact Projection and Basic Assertion\nAuthoring (a real capability gap blocking basic KG usability, not contingent on the UI existing\nfirst). `Aperas-design.md`'s roadmap and `Aperas-dev-status.md` updated to match.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Document Root",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001"
    ],
    "parent": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX2HG000",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Aperas Substrate Architecture Specification (Phase 0)",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G002",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G003",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R002",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00P",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R011",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R018"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G000",
    "text": "Technical reference for the Phase 0 TerminusDB substrate implementation, canonical JSON-LD schema design, AST transduction pipelines, backup mechanisms, and cross-machine synchronization protocols.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G002",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G002",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 1. System Paradigm & Repository Layout",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G004",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G008"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Architectural Paradigm",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G003",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G005",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G006",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G007"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G004",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005/props/StringProp/Cx021lo5cw__XUhc",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005/props/StringProp/YkG30X72TRPL7vnW",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "- **Apeiron (Fluid Core Substrate)**: Schema-free semantic continuum — Markdown content as an unbounded fractal tree, not a fixed document/block hierarchy.\n- **Peras (Crystallized Interfaces)**: Typed boundary structures. As of the fractal-ontology redesign, the whole `BlockNode` tree is eagerly parsed and committed on ingest, each block assigned a Snowflake-generated identity independent of its content or offsets, rather than reified lazily on-demand — the on-demand-reification mechanism (`SpanNode`, character-offset spans) described in earlier revisions of this doc was eliminated, not merely deferred.",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G006",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G006",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005",
    "text": "**Apeiron (Fluid Core Substrate)**: Schema-free semantic continuum — Markdown content as an unbounded fractal tree, not a fixed document/block hierarchy.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G007",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G007",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G005",
    "text": "**Peras (Crystallized Interfaces)**: Typed boundary structures. As of the fractal-ontology redesign, the whole `BlockNode` tree is eagerly parsed and committed on ingest, each block assigned a Snowflake-generated identity independent of its content or offsets, rather than reified lazily on-demand — the on-demand-reification mechanism (`SpanNode`, character-offset spans) described in earlier revisions of this doc was eliminated, not merely deferred.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Directory Structure: Core vs Community Boundaries",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G009",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00A"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G003",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G009",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G009",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G008",
    "text": "```\nAperas/                               # Core Engine (Maintained by Core Dev Team)\n├── scripts/                          # Universal infrastructure & DB operational tooling\n│   ├── restore.sh                    # Backup, restore & verification suite\n│   ├── tdb-log.sh                    # Local-time commit log helper (default count: 20)\n│   └── tdb-doc.sh                    # Local-time document inspection helper\n├── skills/                           # Core agent skill definitions\n│   └── terminusdb/                   # TerminusDB operational reference skill\n├── web/                              # TypeScript project for substrate transducers & UI\n│   └── src/lib/                      # Core data access, AST transducer & schema modules\n│\n└── AperasKG/                         # Domain KG (Maintained by Community)\n    ├── artifacts/                    # Plain-text Markdown domain projections & documentation\n    ├── Apeiron/                      # Portable JSON-LD substrate mirror (schema + instances), bidirectional — see §5\n    ├── schema/                       # Domain-specific JSON-LD schemas extending core\n    ├── ontology/                     # Domain-specific predicate taxonomy / vocabularies\n    └── transducers/                  # Domain-specific ingestion/parsing scripts\n```",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G00A",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G00A",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G008",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 2. Canonical Data Substrate & Schema",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00C",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00D",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R000",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R001"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "text": "The canonical schema is implemented in `web/src/lib/schema.json` (pure JSON-LD, no longer duplicated as TypeScript interfaces) using a fractal, content-addressed class lineage — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` for the full rationale:",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G00C",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G00C",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "text": "| JSON-LD Class | Key Strategy | Core Fields | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `BaseNode` | — (abstract) | `links: Set<BaseLink>` | Root of all addressable content; owns intrinsic links. |\n| `BaseLink` | — (abstract) | `target: BaseNode`, `predicate` | Intrinsic connection authored inside a node. |\n| `BaseEdge` | — (abstract) | `source: BaseNode` (+ `BaseLink` fields) | Extrinsic assertion, independently authored/floating. |\n| `Assertion` | — (concrete, no own fields) | inherits `BaseEdge` | The one concrete extrinsic-edge leaf type — `BaseEdge` is abstract, so something instantiable is needed to actually write edges like `impacts`/`verifies`/`affects`. See `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.C. |\n| `BlockNode` | Lexical (`blockId`, Snowflake-generated) | `blockId`, `title`, `text`, `children: List<BlockNode>`, `unfolded` | Fractal content atom — a document is just the root `BlockNode` of its `ArtifactNode`; no separate `DocumentNode`. |\n| `ArtifactNode` | Lexical (`path`) | `path`, `fileHash`, `lastTrackedAt`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt`, `root: BlockNode` | Metadata index for tracking repository files and hash deltas; anchors the fractal tree. `fileHash`/`ingestedHash` are flat file-content hashes, not structural — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B. |\n| `FolderNode` | Lexical (`path`) | `title`, `path`, `text`, `children: List<BaseNode>` | Structural container mirroring a directory under `AperasKG/artifacts/`; absorbs its own `README.md` (never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`) and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. See `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A. |",
    "type": "table",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53G00D",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53G00D",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "text": "> **Design note**: `BlockNode` identity is a Snowflake-style generated id (see `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts`), not a content hash — decoupling node identity from content fingerprinting was the resolution to the identity/dedup conflation documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F.\n>\n> **Superseded**: `DocumentNode`, `SpanNode`, and `TripleAssertion` (Lexical/Random-keyed, positional `blockId`s) were the Phase 0 schema before this redesign — eliminated entirely, not merely renamed.",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R000",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R000",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "text": "> **Schema Protocol Requirement**: Schema initialization uses `full_replace` for idempotent updates. The submitted schema array **must include an explicit `@context` document** (`@base: \"terminusdb:///data/\"`, `@schema: \"terminusdb:///schema#\"`), or the server will reject the replacement.",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R001",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R001",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G00B",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 3. Data Access & Transduction Modules",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R002",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R003",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R004",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R005"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R003",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R003",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R002",
    "text": "| Module | Location | Responsibilities & Protocol Constraints |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Client Manager** | `web/src/lib/client.ts` | Configures `TerminusDB.WOQLClient`, creates `aperas` database, applies idempotent schema initialization via `full_replace` from `schema.json`. |\n| **Node Identity** | `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` | Generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style `blockId` (timestamp + machine identity + sequence, 13-char Crockford Base32) — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.A. |\n| **AST Transducer** | `web/src/lib/astParser.ts` | Uses `unified.js` (`remark-parse`) to recursively convert Markdown into a nested `BlockNode` tree, assigning each block a fresh Snowflake id via `snowflake.ts` (identity is never derived from content or position). |\n| **Artifact Tracking & Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/artifacts.ts` | Computes `fileHash`, tracks/upserts lightweight `ArtifactNode`s, and ingests the full `BlockNode` tree on change — see §4 below. |\n| **Folder Ingestion** | `web/src/lib/folders.ts` | Walks `AperasKG/artifacts/` and commits the `FolderNode` structural tree — see §4 below. |\n| **Extrinsic Assertion CRUD** | `web/src/lib/crud.ts` | `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the concrete `Assertion` type (source/predicate/target, node-typed per §3 of the design doc's rejection of the `xsd:string` anti-pattern), plus generic best-effort document delete helpers. |\n| **WOQL Engine** | `web/src/lib/woql.ts` | Builds and executes WOQL queries over `Assertion` — `queryNodeAssertions` (both directions) and `traceImpactPropagation` (one-hop sweep along a predicate like `impacts`). |\n| **GraphQL Client** | `web/src/lib/graphql.ts` | `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` fetches an `ArtifactNode` and its full nested `BlockNode` tree (bounded depth) via the auto-generated GraphQL endpoint — see the note below on why this is the *only* full-tree read path. |\n| **Version Control** | `web/src/lib/versionControl.ts` | Manages branches, temporal commit histories, version diffing, merge applications (`apply`), and state resets. Class-agnostic — unaffected by the schema redesign. |\n| **JSON-LD Import/Export** | `web/src/lib/export.ts` | `exportJsonLd`/`importJsonLd` mirror the current schema plus every instance document (per class) between TerminusDB and plain JSON-LD files in `AperasKG/Apeiron/` — see §5. |",
    "type": "table",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R004",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R004",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R002",
    "text": "> **Read-path note**: `client.getDocument()` on an `ArtifactNode` returns `root` as a bare reference id string, not the nested tree, and likewise for `BlockNode.children`. This is *not* because `@subdocument` is required for unfolding (a natural-sounding but wrong assumption we initially made) — it's simply that `BlockNode` isn't schema-annotated as unfoldable. TerminusDB has two independent schema-level annotations that control this: property-level `\"@unfold\": true` and class-level `\"@unfoldable\": []`. We benchmarked marking `BlockNode` class-level `@unfoldable` (which does work, including through the recursive `List<BlockNode>` children) against the real 149-block `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` tree, and it was ~3.5x slower than `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL`'s GraphQL query (~48ms vs ~13.5ms steady-state) — so we kept GraphQL as the tree-read path rather than adopting it. Separately, we found that the *property-level* `\"@unfold\": true` variant silently does nothing on `List`-typed fields specifically (works on `Set`/`Optional`/`Cardinality`) — an upstream bug, filed as [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512), traced to `List`'s internal RDF-linked-list (`Cons`/`rdf:first`/`rdf:rest`) representation not being reachable from the property-level unfold check. That bug doesn't affect our decision (we'd have used class-level `@unfoldable`, which is unaffected), but is a useful data point that this part of TerminusDB is new and still maturing.",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R005",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R005",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R002",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 4. Artifact Tracking & Ingestion Pipeline",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R007",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R008",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R009"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006/props/StringProp/CQXI00TShR6DW_Dm",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006/props/StringProp/kYxddywD704cF0yq",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "text": "Managed via `web/src/lib/artifacts.ts` and CLI entrypoint `web/src/lib/kgCli.ts`:",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R007",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R007",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006",
    "text": "**Lightweight Registration (`npm run kg:track`)**:\n  Computes content hashes for files under `AperasKG/artifacts/` and upserts lightweight `ArtifactNode` records — a no-op skip (no KG write at all) when the hash is unchanged, so unscoped sweeps (e.g. the `post-index-change` hook) stay cheap.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R008",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R008",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006",
    "text": "**Incremental Ingestion (`npm run kg:ingest`)**:\n  Compares current file content hash (`fileHash`) against stored `ingestedHash`. If changed, parses Markdown into a nested `BlockNode` tree (fresh Snowflake ids throughout) and commits it via a single `ArtifactNode.root` update — TerminusDB recursively ingests the whole tree in one operation. Re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact currently orphans its entire previous tree rather than reusing unchanged blocks' ids — acceptable for now since ingestion targets uningested artifacts; cross-ingestion identity matching is unimplemented (see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F).\n  Also rebuilds the `FolderNode` structural tree (`web/src/lib/folders.ts`) in the same run: one `FolderNode` per directory under `AperasKG/artifacts/`, each absorbing its own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's own children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`) and referencing nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. The whole folder tree is committed as a single nested write from the artifacts root each run — cheap, since it's directory-count-sized, not content-sized.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R009",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R009",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R006",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 5. JSON-LD Substrate Import/Export",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00B",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00F",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00G"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "text": "`web/src/lib/export.ts`, wired through `kgCli.ts`, bidirectionally mirrors the schema and every instance document between TerminusDB and plain JSON-LD files in `AperasKG/Apeiron/`:",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00B",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00B",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "text": "| File | Contents |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `schema.jsonld` | The full schema graph (`getDocument({ graph_type: 'schema' })`), verbatim. |\n| `ArtifactNode.jsonld`, `FolderNode.jsonld`, `BlockNode.jsonld`, `Assertion.jsonld` | One file per instance class — a leading `@context` document, then every live (`getDocument({ type, as_list: true })`) instance of that class, sorted by id for diff-stable re-exports. |",
    "type": "table",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00C",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00D",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00E"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C/props/StringProp/52uXHmZjBbgiKffb",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C/props/StringProp/gD5sGN3O_WpB3lFQ",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "- **`npm run kg:export`** — writes all of the above from the current TerminusDB state, overwriting the files.\n- **`npm run kg:import`** — reads the files back: applies `schema.jsonld` via `full_replace`, then upserts each class's instances (every document already carries its own `@id`, so a matching document is updated in place, not duplicated). Each class is submitted as a single batched `updateDocument` call, in the dependency order `BlockNode` → `ArtifactNode` → `FolderNode` → `Assertion`, so a document is never written before something it references — `BlockNode`'s own parent/child references resolve within its own batch (one commit, so intra-batch forward references are fine); everything after it can then safely reference already-committed ids. Every write is its own TerminusDB commit, so before writing the schema or a given class, its content hash is compared (`hashDocSet` in `client.ts` — the same order-independent hash already used to skip a no-op schema apply) against what's currently live, and the write is skipped entirely when nothing changed, rather than landing a no-op commit.",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00D",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00D",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C",
    "text": "**`npm run kg:export`** — writes all of the above from the current TerminusDB state, overwriting the files.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00E",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00E",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00C",
    "text": "**`npm run kg:import`** — reads the files back: applies `schema.jsonld` via `full_replace`, then upserts each class's instances (every document already carries its own `@id`, so a matching document is updated in place, not duplicated). Each class is submitted as a single batched `updateDocument` call, in the dependency order `BlockNode` → `ArtifactNode` → `FolderNode` → `Assertion`, so a document is never written before something it references — `BlockNode`'s own parent/child references resolve within its own batch (one commit, so intra-batch forward references are fine); everything after it can then safely reference already-committed ids. Every write is its own TerminusDB commit, so before writing the schema or a given class, its content hash is compared (`hashDocSet` in `client.ts` — the same order-independent hash already used to skip a no-op schema apply) against what's currently live, and the write is skipped entirely when nothing changed, rather than landing a no-op commit.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Purpose: how `AperasKG` holds a backup of its own KG",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00F",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "text": "This round-trip — not a TerminusDB-level backup — is the correct answer to \"how does `AperasKG` hold a record of its KG,\" per its original design goal of storing both the artifacts and the KG. `AperasKG/Apeiron/` is the canonical graph content, materialized as plain, diffable JSON-LD text and committed to the same git repository as `AperasKG/artifacts/` — an ordinary `git commit` over that directory *is* the KG's backup, with all the history, diffing, and portability that implies, and `kg:import` is the restore path (bootstrap a fresh database, or recover state) back out of it. This also happens to make the content engine-agnostic — `AperasKG/Apeiron/` is a snapshot any future substrate engine could read without a bespoke migration script (see `Aperas-design.md`'s Development Roadmap, \"Phase 4: Substrate Evolution\") — but that's a secondary benefit of the same design, not the primary reason it exists.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Scope and non-goals",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00N"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00A",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00J",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00K",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00M"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00G",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H/props/StringProp/sVZN3bk89JR0RE9P",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H/props/StringProp/tV-rEQdqm36RShZ5",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "text": "- **Flat, not nested.** Instances are dumped and read back exactly as `getDocument`/`updateDocument` handle them — `BlockNode.children` and `ArtifactNode.root` are reference ids, not inlined subtrees (see §2's \"Read-path note\"), matching how TerminusDB itself stores documents and keeping per-class diffs scoped to that class alone.\n- **Includes tombstoned documents.** The export/import round-trip is a full audit snapshot, not a live-only view — reconciliation's `tombstonedAt` markers (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`) are preserved rather than filtered out.\n- **Whole-class granularity, not a merge.** Import upserts every document in a class file; it doesn't diff against the live database or reconcile divergence — reconciliation (`reconcile.ts`) only ever runs against `AperasKG/artifacts/` content during `kg:ingest`, not against this export/import path.",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00J",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00J",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "text": "**Flat, not nested.** Instances are dumped and read back exactly as `getDocument`/`updateDocument` handle them — `BlockNode.children` and `ArtifactNode.root` are reference ids, not inlined subtrees (see §2's \"Read-path note\"), matching how TerminusDB itself stores documents and keeping per-class diffs scoped to that class alone.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00K",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00K",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "text": "**Includes tombstoned documents.** The export/import round-trip is a full audit snapshot, not a live-only view — reconciliation's `tombstonedAt` markers (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`) are preserved rather than filtered out.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00M",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00M",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00H",
    "text": "**Whole-class granularity, not a merge.** Import upserts every document in a class file; it doesn't diff against the live database or reconcile divergence — reconciliation (`reconcile.ts`) only ever runs against `AperasKG/artifacts/` content during `kg:ingest`, not against this export/import path.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00N",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00N",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00G",
    "text": "---",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## 6. TerminusDB Server Operational Backup",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00Q",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00W"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53G001",
    "text": "This section is server infrastructure for the TerminusDB instance itself — Docker-volume-level disaster recovery, unrelated to `AperasKG`'s own record of its content. It answers \"how do I recover this TerminusDB server if its volume is lost,\" not \"how does `AperasKG` hold a backup of its KG.\" That second question is answered by §5: `AperasKG/Apeiron/` plus `kg:export`/`kg:import`, git-tracked alongside `AperasKG/artifacts/` like any other content in the domain-KG repo — not by storing TerminusDB-level snapshots in or near `AperasKG` at all, which an earlier design iteration tried (`db/` briefly lived under `AperasKG/`) before being reconsidered as the wrong coupling: a git-tracked domain repo has no good way to diff, merge, or meaningfully version an opaque binary DB snapshot, and (per the investigation below) those snapshots aren't even portable between independent TerminusDB stores.",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Whole-Volume Disaster Recovery (`restore.sh backup-full | verify-full | restore-full`)",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00P",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00S",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00T",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00V"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00Q",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R/props/StringProp/NvlZy6ySDGhnr39v",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R/props/StringProp/_hfkCo-hq6yDop-N",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "text": "- **Primary Adopted Method**: Creates a tarball of the backing Docker volume `terminusdb_storage` via a temporary Alpine container with the TerminusDB container temporarily stopped to ensure on-disk head consistency.\n- **Scope**: **Cross-Machine Host Transfer**.\n- **Restore Safety**: `restore-full` extracts into an isolated temporary volume/container (`<container>-restored`) for inspection. Automatic promotion (`--overwrite`) updates container volume bindings with automatic fallback to `-old` on startup failure.",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00S",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00S",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "text": "**Primary Adopted Method**: Creates a tarball of the backing Docker volume `terminusdb_storage` via a temporary Alpine container with the TerminusDB container temporarily stopped to ensure on-disk head consistency.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00T",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00T",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "text": "**Scope**: **Cross-Machine Host Transfer**.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZ53R00V",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZ53R00V",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00R",
    "text": "**Restore Safety**: `restore-full` extracts into an isolated temporary volume/container (`<container>-restored`) for inspection. Automatic promotion (`--overwrite`) updates container volume bindings with automatic fallback to `-old` on startup failure.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ53R00W",
