    "text": "**Fixed**: `kg:ingest` used to double-ingest `README.md`. `listArtifactFiles` (`artifacts.ts`) walked every `.md` file with no README exclusion, so `ingestAllArtifacts` ingested a directory's `README.md` as an ordinary `ArtifactNode`+`BlockNode` tree — in addition to, and completely independently of, `folders.ts`'s `buildFolderTree`, which separately parses the same file and correctly folds its content into the owning `FolderNode`. Reproduced live before fixing: a real `README.md` produced both a correct `FolderNode`-absorbed copy and a separate stray `ArtifactNode`. Root cause: `artifacts.ts` and `folders.ts` each walked `AperasKG/artifacts/` with their own file-listing logic, only one of which knew to skip README files. Fixed by factoring one shared `isReadmeFilename` predicate into `artifacts.ts` (which `folders.ts` now imports instead of its own local constant) and applying it in `listArtifactFiles` — plus the same guard added to `kg:track`'s explicit single-file path (`kgCli.ts`), which bypasses that list entirely and needed its own check.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000A",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000A",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0006",
    "text": "Automated tracking trigger (`AperasKG/.githooks/post-commit`, `post-index-change`) — done: `post-commit` auto-runs a scoped `kg:track` on commit, `post-index-change` auto-runs a full `kg:track` sweep on branch checkout / `git reset` (including `--hard`, which fires no hook of its own) — `post-checkout` was tried too but dropped as redundant once `post-index-change` was confirmed to fire alongside it with equivalent coverage.",
    "type": "listItem",
