    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0006",
    "text": "Cross-machine remotes — **done**: reciprocal SSH-tunneled TerminusDB remotes (reciprocal remote endpoints), `fetch` confirmed both directions. `push`/`pull` themselves only fast-forward and fail with `no_common_history` once both sides have diverged past their common point (no `--force` flag exists either) — reconciliation is `rebase` (replays one side's divergent commits onto a base built from the other, see `tdb-cli-status-walkthrough.md` §6) or, for a deliberate discard-and-replace sync, `reset` directly onto a fetched commit id (§7, reciprocal in both directions, no intermediate branch needed). Both live-verified against the real `aperas` DB: rebased a 9-commit remote-derived branch onto local `main`'s 1120 commits (zero conflicts; the reverse direction hangs — direction matters, see §6.2), then promoted `main` to the reconciled 1129-commit tip via `reset`.",
