    ],
    "text": "**RESOLVED** Design issue: \"AperasKG stores the KG\" was answered with a DB backup, not a KG export — corrected",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000G",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000G",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000F",
    "text": "`AperasKG` was designed to hold both the domain artifacts and the KG itself, but the KG lives in a DB — so the earlier approach to fulfilling that second half was to associate whole-TerminusDB-volume/bundle backups (`restore.sh`, briefly stored under `AperasKG/db/`) with the domain-KG repo. That coupling was the wrong move: a git-tracked repo has no good way to diff, merge, or meaningfully version an opaque binary DB snapshot, and (per the `#2509` investigation above) those snapshots turned out not to even be portable between independent TerminusDB stores — so it wasn't a viable backup path for `AperasKG` even setting the git-coupling problem aside.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000H",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000H",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000F",
    "text": "Corrected via the JSON-LD import/export round-trip (`web/src/lib/export.ts`, `kg:export`/`kg:import`, `Aperas-architecture.md` §5): `AperasKG/Apeiron/` holds the canonical graph content as plain, diffable JSON-LD text, committed to the same repo as `AperasKG/artifacts/` — an ordinary `git commit` over that directory is now the KG's backup, `kg:import` is the restore path.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000J",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000J",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000F",
    "text": "`restore.sh`'s whole-volume/bundle mechanism (§6) is unaffected and stays as-is — it's TerminusDB server infrastructure (Docker-volume disaster recovery), a different, unrelated concern from how `AperasKG` records its own content. Likewise, the SSH-tunneled TerminusDB remotes (§7) are unrelated to `AperasKG` — that's cross-machine sync for the TerminusDB server itself, not something this redesign touches.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000K",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000K",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0004",
    "text": "**Fixed**: TerminusDB database renamed `aperas_apeiron` → `aperas` — the `aperas_` prefix was project-namespacing for a database name that already only ever means one thing on this dedicated instance, and `Apeiron` names a philosophical/architectural role (the fluid core substrate), not a resource identifier; naming the database after the project itself was simpler and avoided that mismatch. Migrated live via the JSON-LD round-trip rather than any TerminusDB-native rename (there isn't one — only `createDatabase`/`deleteDatabase`): `kg:export` from the old database, `kg:import` into a freshly created `aperas`, content parity verified class-by-class via the same order-independent `hashDocSet` hash `kg:import`'s own skip-if-unchanged check uses (all 5 matched: schema, `ArtifactNode`, `BlockNode`, `FolderNode`, `Assertion`), then the old `aperas_apeiron` database deleted. All defaults (`client.ts`, `tdb-log.sh`, `tdb-doc.sh`, `restore.sh`) and doc mentions updated to match.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000M",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000M",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0004",
    "text": "**Fixed**: full migration to the fractal ontology, `FolderNode` implemented, `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both passing (see \"RESOLVED\" entries below for detail).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000N",
