    "text": "**RESOLVED** Design issue: Positional identity replaced by Fractal Ontology",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000Q",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000Q",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "The legacy flat `DocumentNode` / `BlockNode` / `SpanNode` schema was entirely eliminated.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000R",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000R",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "Designed and implemented a universal, recursive `BlockNode` topology (Fractal Ontology) rooted in `ArtifactNode`.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000S",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000S",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "Schema updated to pure JSON-LD (`schema.json`), avoiding TypeScript interface duplication.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000T",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000T",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "IDs & content fingerprint — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1). `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style identifier (timestamp + machine identity w/ personal failover + sequence counter, 13-char Crockford Base32); `astParser.ts` uses it for every `blockId` instead of the old content hash. `ArtifactNode.contentHash` renamed to `fileHash` throughout (`artifacts.ts`, `schema.json`) to match §1.B's file-domain-only fingerprint — no structural/recursive hash. Verified live: cleared stale pre-redesign `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode` docs, ran `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` across all 8 artifacts (1144 blocks total, including a 648-block single-artifact burst), zero id collisions. Also found and fixed a real pre-existing bug while verifying: `getArtifactRecord` treated a missing document's raw 404 response (a string, not a thrown error) as a valid record, so untracked artifacts silently reported \"unchanged\" instead of erroring. Reconciliation (best-effort content matching, §1.C history in Appendix F) remains unimplemented — no code needed it yet, since ingestion so far has only ever run against uningested artifacts.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000V",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000V",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "Ingestion (`astParser.ts` and `artifacts.ts`) now parses Markdown into a deeply nested tree structure and commits the entire fractal tree via `ArtifactNode.root` in a single TerminusDB operation. Note: a plain `getDocument` read only ever returns `root`/`children` as reference ids, not the nested tree, so full-tree reads go through `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`) instead — deliberately, not because the Document API is incapable of it (see `Aperas-architecture.md` §2's \"Read-path note\" for the full investigation, including a filed upstream bug, [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512)).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000W",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000W",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` are now Snowflake-keyed (`folderId`/`artifactId`), `path` a plain mutable field — see the \"Reconciliation matching\" entry below for the full migration.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000X",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000X",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "`crud.ts`/`woql.ts`/`graphql.ts`/`verifyPhase0.ts` — **migrated off the dead pre-redesign schema and live-verified**. `crud.ts` now provides `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the new `Assertion` type; `woql.ts` queries `Assertion.source`/`predicate`/`target` (node-typed, not the old flat `xsd:string` `subjectId`/`objectId`) in both directions plus one-hop impact propagation; `graphql.ts` replaced the removed `docId`-scoped block query with `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (bounded-depth nested `root`/`children` selection — GraphQL has no native recursion, so depth is generated explicitly, default 10). `verifyPhase0.ts` was rewritten into a full idempotent, self-cleaning live test of the whole pipeline (AST parsing → track/ingest → GraphQL tree read → `FolderNode` ingestion → `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL traversal → temporal commit management); `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both confirmed passing.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000Y",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000Y",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Discovered while wiring this up**: TerminusDB enforces referential integrity on document delete — deleting a still-referenced document (e.g. an `ArtifactNode` still listed in a `FolderNode.children`, or a `BlockNode` still pointed to by `ArtifactNode.root`) fails with a `SchemaCheckFailure`, not silently. The best-effort delete helpers in `crud.ts` (`deleteDocumentIfExists`/`deleteDocumentsIfExist`) used to swallow *all* errors on the assumption only \"not found\" could occur — that assumption was wrong and masked this failure mode; they now log instead of swallowing silently, and any caller managing referenced state (like `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup) has to delete in reverse-reference order.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS000Z",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS000Z",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Heading levels now define tree structure** — **implemented and live-verified**. `astParser.ts` gained `groupByHeadings`, a one-pass depth-stack transform run on every flat mdast sibling list before conversion: each heading becomes the parent of everything until a heading of depth <= its own. A doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` now parses as nested (`Title` containing `Section A`, `Section B`, each with their own body), not a flat list under the root. Alongside this: every `BlockNode` now carries its raw mdast `type` (needed by reconciliation's leaf/container split below), and `list`/`listItem`/`blockquote` no longer carry the full-subtree-duplicate `text` they used to (confirmed live pre-fix: a `listItem`'s `text` byte-for-byte duplicated its own paragraph child's) — containers now carry no content of their own, by design.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0010",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0010",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G). New `web/src/lib/reconcile.ts`: a Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff — the longest-common-run algorithm behind Python's `difflib` — applied two-stage per level (Stage A anchors on leaf content by `heading XOR text`; Stage B aligns containers by type within the segments Stage A's anchors define), with ambiguous same-content duplicates declined rather than guessed. Matched `BlockNode`s reuse their old `blockId`; unmatched old ones get an explicit `tombstonedAt` (new field on `BaseNode`, inherited everywhere) rather than being silently orphaned; a block relocated to a different section is detected as a cross-parent move via the same mechanism, one level up from per-parent matching. `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` moved off `Lexical`-on-`path` to Snowflake ids (`artifactId`/`folderId`, same scheme as `BlockNode.blockId`), `path` now a plain mutable field with `title`/`text` added to `ArtifactNode` (filename / naive first-paragraph abstract, matching `FolderNode`'s existing shape) — this is what makes a file/folder rename a field update instead of a delete-and-recreate. Rename detection reuses the identical Gestalt-matching primitive one level up: on every `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` sweep, disk-only and DB-only leftover paths are matched by abstract-text similarity (`matchLeftoverByAbstract`) before falling back to plain add/remove. Wired into `ingestArtifact` (fires whenever a prior ingestion exists), `trackAllArtifacts`, and `ingestFolderTree`; `kgCli.ts` reports renamed/removed/reconciled counts alongside the existing tracked/ingested counts. Live-verified via `verifyPhase0.ts` (edit-and-reingest keeps unrelated `blockId`s stable, reports sane unchanged/added counts) and a manual rename test against a throwaway artifact (`artifactId` and `blockId`s survived a real on-disk move). Migrating the key scheme required clearing all pre-existing `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`/`BlockNode` documents first, since TerminusDB rejects a schema whose new required fields the old instance data doesn't have — the whole KG was then rebuilt from `AperasKG/artifacts/` via a full `kg:track` + `kg:ingest` sweep, per the project's disk-is-source-of-truth model.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0011",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0011",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Artifact Projection** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 1 of 3). New `web/src/lib/project.ts` serializes an `ArtifactNode`'s ingested `BlockNode` tree back into Markdown — canonical regeneration, not byte-exact: headings/paragraphs/code round-trip via their raw `title`/`text`, while `list`/`blockquote` are regenerated as clean Markdown (list items always blank-line-separated regardless of original tight/loose style; blockquote `> ` re-prefixed uniformly rather than trusting what the raw text happens to carry). Needed two new captured fields on `BlockNode` — `ordered`/`start` (list numbering) and `checked` (task-list checkbox) — both `Optional`, so unlike the `artifactId`/`type` migration this needed no DB wipe. Exposed via `npm run kg:project -- <path>`. Verified two ways: `verifyPhase0.ts`'s synthetic sample (every branch: ordered/unordered/task lists, nested list, blockquote, code) round-trips with zero drift by reusing `reconcile.ts`'s own matcher as the equivalence check; and, more usefully, running the same check against all 11 real artifacts in `AperasKG/artifacts/` surfaced two genuine bugs no synthetic sample had exercised — a nested code fence's closing `` ``` `` desyncing from its opening one because only a multi-line leaf's *first* line has container-required indentation stripped (every later line keeps its literal original-file column; fixed with a `dedent` normalization), and an *indented* (4-space) code block silently degrading into an ordinary paragraph because its raw slice carries no fence to re-emit (fixed by re-fencing it). After those two fixes, 9 of 11 real artifacts round-trip with zero drift; the other 2 each show one accepted, disclosed difference (absolute code-indentation depth normalized to the minimum; indented-style converted to fenced-style) — real content changes under exact-key matching, not bugs, per the design doc §8.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0012",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0012",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Basic Assertion Authoring** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`). New `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI commands (`kgCli.ts`) let a human or agent actually write and inspect a real `Assertion` — previously the only thing that ever called `insertAssertion` was a hardcoded synthetic edge in `verifyPhase0.ts`'s test harness. `source`/`target` accept either a full node id (direct addressing) or a bare artifact/folder path (query-based addressing, resolved via `getArtifactRecord`/the new `getFolderRecord`, artifact tried first since the two never collide) — block-level assertions stay direct-id-only; closing that gap became its own effort, see \"Agentic Query Tools\" below. New narrow `deleteAssertion` (`crud.ts`) does exact source/predicate/target deletion, distinct from the existing blunt `deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` (kept for demo/reset cleanup only). Live end-to-end test against two real artifacts (assert → list → unassert → list-empty) surfaced one real bug: WOQL binds a literal-typed field (`predicate`, `xsd:string`) as a wrapped `{\"@type\", \"@value\"}` object rather than a plain string, unlike node-typed `source`/`target` bindings — `kg:assertions` printed `[object Object]` until fixed with an `unwrapLiteral` helper in `woql.ts`'s `queryNodeAssertions`. Never caught by `verifyPhase0.ts`'s existing Assertion test because that only checks binding presence/membership, never a literal field's actual value. Reordered from Phase 2 into Phase 0 itself (not merely Phase 1) per `Aperas-design.md`'s roadmap, so Phase 1 skill-building starts with it already available.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0013",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0013",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0014",
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0015"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0013/props/StringProp/1Uh_ZGWTbkHOKKmz",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0013/props/StringProp/DUKPeiv1pF29esC5",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "text": "**Agentic Query Tools** — reordered from Phase 1 into Phase 0, design settled (`Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**. Three CLI tools closing the block-level addressing gap Basic Assertion Authoring (above) left open, and making mode 3 of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A concrete for the first time: `kg:tree` (a deep structural map — depth-first with an optional depth bound; title-only by default), `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` (the actual breadth-first primitive: one level, full content, the first code to ever give the long-inert `unfolded` flag a real effect), and `kg:search` (keyword/regex content search via `WOQL.re` — two unrestricted `title`/`text` queries rather than one per class, since the property names are shared across all three node classes and the id prefix alone already reveals kind). Smoke-tested against the real KG (`kg:tree`, `kg:search`, an `unfold`/`fold` round-trip on a real `BlockNode`, `kg:project`).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0014",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0014",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0013",
    "text": "**`unfolded` promoted from `BlockNode` to `BaseNode`** (§4.1) — the field had only ever lived on `BlockNode`, a leftover from before `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` existed as separate concrete classes rather than a deliberate restriction. `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` now persist real state against any node kind, not just display normally with nothing to save for the other two. `kg:tree --unfolded` renders the *combined* shape a sequence of `kg:fold`/`kg:unfold` calls leaves behind in one walk instead of separate scrollback: a node prints full `text` instead of `title` exactly when its own parent has `unfolded === true`, recursion stops at a folded node (with a `(folded — kg:unfold <id> to expand)` hint naming the exact fix), and the walk's own root always stays title-only — composes with `--depth`/`--no-holders` unchanged.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
