  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0015",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0015",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0013",
    "text": "**Real bug found live during this promotion**: `trackArtifact`'s (`artifacts.ts`) and `buildFolderTree`'s (`folders.ts`) record-rebuild paths already carry forward fields like `text`/`root`/`ingestedHash` from the previous document on every re-track/re-ingest, but neither had ever needed to carry forward a *view-state* field before — `unfolded` would have been silently reset to folded on the very next `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` of an `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`, the same class of regression `reconcile.ts` was already fixed for on `BlockNode`. Fixed by adding `unfolded` to `normalizeArtifactDoc`'s carried-forward field set and threading `existingByPath` into `buildFolderTree` (which, unlike `ArtifactNode`, rebuilds its whole tree fresh from disk every run rather than reusing a stored record, so it has nothing to carry forward from without an explicit lookup). Confirmed live: unfolded an `ArtifactNode`, forced a real re-track (content hash change), and it stayed unfolded; same for a `FolderNode` across a direct `ingestFolderTree` re-run.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0016",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0016",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS000P",
    "text": "**Markdown → Fractal Tree Mapping** (`Aperas-markdown-fractal-mapping-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**: `heading`/`listItem` now *consume* (not copy) their leading paragraph as `text`, shallow, one node fewer per section; a `list` now dissolves into whichever `paragraph`/`listItem`/`heading` immediately precedes it (`orderedList`/`startIndex` becoming that adopting node's own `props`) rather than remaining a standalone node, orphaned only when nothing valid precedes it — including the case, found while implementing this, where two lists sit directly adjacent to each other (the second is orphaned, since a `list` itself is never a valid adoption anchor); a new generic `Prop`/`StringProp` mechanism (`BaseNode.props: Set<Prop>`, `props.ts`'s shared `getProp`/`setProp`) replaces the one-field-per-feature pattern, `orderedList`/`startIndex`/`checked` all migrated onto it; YAML frontmatter is extracted via `remark-frontmatter` and stored as one `props` entry on both `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` (`parseMarkdownTree` now returns `{root, frontmatter?}`); `folders.ts`'s README absorption got the same copy-to-consume fix. `project.ts`'s serializer was generalized to match: `heading`/`listItem` emit their consumed `text` before their children, and `renderChildren` scans for contiguous `listItem` runs anywhere in a node's children (not just a dedicated `list` case) using that node's own `props` for numbering. One real GraphQL wrinkle surfaced and fixed: `props: Set<Prop>` can't be queried with an inline fragment on `StringProp` (TerminusDB's generated GraphQL schema makes `Prop` its own concrete type, not an interface `StringProp` implements) — worked around via the generic `_json` field every generated type carries, parsed back into `{key, value}` by `graphql.ts`'s `normalizeProps`. `verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both clean. Same known limitation as Artifact Projection/Agentic Query Tools above: already-ingested real artifacts won't reflect any of this until something forces their re-ingestion.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0017",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0017",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0004",
    "text": "**Interactive Title & Cross-Link Authoring** (`Aperas-interactive-summarization-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**. Resolves Stage 2 item 5 below (`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md`, \"AI-driven summarization... splitting blocks into `title` vs `text`\") — reframed per the project's own zero-background-API principle (`Aperas-design.md` Phase 3 rationale): no LLM call, the CLI just asks whoever is running it (human or an already-in-the-loop coding agent) directly. New `kg:title`/`kg:link` (`kgCli.ts`) prompt interactively for a real title on any still-unlabeled `BlockNode`, or cross-links a block's prose makes that wikilink-syntax extraction (`astParser.ts:92-106`) doesn't catch; both share a new `updateBlockNode` fetch-merge-replace primitive (`crud.ts`) since none existed before. A real regression this design surfaced and fixed before it could ship: `reconcileNode` (`reconcile.ts`) only carried `blockId` forward for a matched (content-unchanged) pair, so a title/link set today would've silently reverted on the artifact's next re-ingest — now carries `title`/`unfolded`/`links` forward too (`carryForwardFields`), and `resolveBlockLinks` (`artifacts.ts`) merges freshly-resolved wikilinks onto that carried-forward `links` instead of overwriting it. Two more bugs found live during this work, both fixed: `graphql.ts`'s block field selection never included `links` at all (so the carry-forward had nothing to carry — added a `links { _id }` selection plus a `normalizeLinks` step converting GraphQL's full-IRI `_id` to the short ref-id form `updateDocument` expects, mirroring the existing `_json`/`normalizeProps` pattern); and `rl.question()` (readline/promises) races against stream-end once real `await`s happen between prompts, which piped/non-interactive stdin (a coding agent driving the tool with pre-computed answers) hits — fixed by consuming the readline interface's own async iterator (`createLineReader`) instead. Live-verified end-to-end: a title and a cross-link set via these commands both survived a real re-ingestion round-trip, confirmed via direct `doc get`, not just the tools' own reported output.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0018",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0019"
    ],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0004",
    "text": "**Deep Path Resolution** (`Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md`) — **implemented and live-verified**, both directions. `kg:path <id>` (id→path): a new `parent: Optional<BaseNode>` field on `BlockNode` (`astParser.ts`'s `stampParents`, re-run post-reconciliation since `carryForwardFields` reassigns `blockId`s), walked upward by `nodeRef.ts`'s `resolveIdToPath` to the owning `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`. `kg:resolve <path>` (path→id, the reverse): extends `nodeRef.ts`'s `resolveNodeRefOrNull` with the full deep-path grammar — `.`/`..`/leading `/` (Linux-flavored relative addressing, `--base <path>` for batch resolution), exact-then-prefix title matching with \"decline rather than guess\" on ambiguity, and `--create-holder` (a tombstone-like placeholder for a target that doesn't exist yet, tail-aligned `--titles` so a caller only supplies titles for segments actually being created) reaching all the way from a single heading up through imagining whole new `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` chains from nothing. Wired into `artifacts.ts`'s wikilink extractor (forward references to not-yet-written headings now resolve to a holder instead of being silently dropped) and backported into `kg:tree`/`kg:search` (a `(holder)` mark, `--no-holders` to filter — transparent for indentation in `kg:tree`, not a subtree prune, since a holder is per-node not per-branch). New `holder: Optional<xsd:boolean>` field on `BaseNode` (not a `Prop` — a first-class concept needed on every node kind, not parser-derived per-node metadata); `ArtifactNode.fileHash`/`lastTrackedAt` made `Optional` to let a holder `ArtifactNode` exist with no real file behind it yet.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00C7BJZHS0019",
    "blockId": "00C7BJZHS0019",
    "children": [],
    "parent": "BlockNode/00C7BJZHS0018",
    "text": "Several real bugs found live during implementation, none of them the original design's own text (all consistent with what `Aperas-deep-path-resolution-design.md` itself now documents inline, §4/§7): a heading's leading `#`/`##` slugifying to leading dashes made prefix matching dead on arrival until the candidate's dashes were stripped before the `startsWith` check; writing a holder directly under an `ArtifactNode` failed schema check because its one child is the singular `root` field, not a `children` List; and, most fundamentally, resolving wikilinks *before* the tree's own write was a genuine chicken-and-egg bug (the implicit base needs an already-persisted `.parent` chain, so anything brand-new in the current edit would resolve against the *previous* ingestion's stale tree) — fixed by moving link resolution to a separate pass after the write, extracting/stripping each block's raw `linkCodes` beforehand since `schema.json` has no such field and leaving it in fails the write itself. `verifyPhase0.ts`'s wikilink test extended to cover all three shapes end-to-end (a bare snowflake code, a forward reference that becomes a real holder, and a still-genuinely-unresolvable one that correctly declines) rather than just the original single self-link case.",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
